--- !u!114 &8364538
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8364536}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8e53287d76a0f7f418ae0767649c5267, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  noteText: 'Assignment:

    Make the door open if the player holds the key, or
    play a locked sound otherwise. Duplicate the door and see what happens.


    Extra
    Challenge 1:

    Create an extra door and key. Any key can open any door but
    only once and then it is consumed!


    Extra Challenge 2:

    Same as before,
    but now key 1 can only open door 1, key 2 can only open door 2!


    Note:

    The
    key already has the correct colliders, and the door already makes a lock sound
    if you hit it.


    Note:

    DON''T apply the changes to any of the Prefabs
    because it will mess up all the other demo scenes. Although in a real life scenario,
    you would apply the changes OR create prefab variants, in this case it also allows
    you to clearly see the CHANGES done in a Scene, with respect to the base prefab.'
  noteType: 0
